## Caps and complete dependency privacy policy

Hard-coded caps, also fixed in policy: 120 seconds wall time, 64 MiB individual
read, 256 MiB total metadata reads including final rechecks, 64 MiB staged
output, 20,000 catalog records, and 1 MiB per public stream. These are collector
limits only; original native/proof clocks and resource limits do not change.
No-follow, single-link regular inputs have inode/size/time stability checked
before/after reading. Writes are exclusive and file/parent fsynced. The terminal
receipt labels staged bytes before its own write; read/time counts include the
final source check. Cap/time exhaustion fails without a passed receipt.

| Dependency set | Exact public retention | Identity-only treatment |
|---|---|---|
| 29 F5 sources, 547 F5 pins, 182 V5 closure, original source reviews/watchers | Existing four accepted archive maps are fixed and referenced | Static identities are inherited from reviewed maps and actual F5; no blanket fresh-rehash assertion |
| Existing archived source, test, failed-preparation, review, integration objects | No duplicate copies | `already-retained-reference` points to exact accepted map/object |
| Original full producer/fresh verifier receipts, two positive proofs, complete input package, two extracted-compiler corpus inventories | Eight exact positive stdout/stderr streams | Receipts, source/corpus file identities and compiler/proof bodies are references; proof/binary bodies never opened |
| Actual watcher and F5 result | Two exact watcher stdout/stderr streams; allowlisted typed F5 summary | Complete original watcher/F5 JSON are private references, not sanitized replacements |
| V5 controller/baseline, per-generation admissions/completions, selected V4 cost, suite histories | Summary states original failed history and exact case partition | Full JSON, nested selected `raw_stdout`, host snapshots and process ownership stay local |
| 42 fresh construct/verify commands | 84 exact stdout/stderr streams, each bounded and privacy-scanned | Original command receipts, input maps and resource logs remain hash references |
| 23 generation/case capacity permits and observation logs | Counts and source-bound scope in summary | Metadata receipts rehashed; observation bodies referenced through their exact permit identities |
| 42 registrations plus original observations/retirements | No raw process tables | All exact metadata identities retained, process records remain private |
| Every nested byte identity in the loaded metadata | None unless explicitly listed above | Classified under its path or original JSON pointer; arbitrary unknown data are reference-only, never copied or followed |
| Signed URLs, credentials, raw host process output, unknown structured payloads | Never | Fail if present in any allowed public stream; no redaction of originals |

`dependencies.json` is the union of the above declared closures and runtime
metadata graph, not an unconstrained filesystem crawl. `observed_metadata_bytes`
means this collector read/rehashed that exact small body. `false` explicitly
means a declared identity from authenticated F5/maps; existence, fresh hashing
or public safety are not inferred. `source-reference`, `private-original-reference`,
`artifact-reference-no-body`, `unreviewed-original-reference` and
`already-retained-reference` all forbid body copying. Only the explicit 94
stream allowlist is `exact-public-stream`. The full public summary is a typed
projection, linked to the original private F5 identity; it is not byte-identical
to that original or an independently replayed acceptance verdict.

The separate `preview.py` performs only static metadata classification. Its
preparation receipt cannot satisfy collector admission. The initial actual
preview classified 14,654 entries using 4,064,325 metadata bytes, including the
6,215-file historical immutable baseline and both complete corpus inventories.
The dynamic final metadata is added only after actual acceptance. Caps stay
fixed; exceeding them needs a new reviewed preparation, not silent widening.

